Meteorological data during the second release of ETEX

file name: TYPEDATE ------->  TYPEMMDDHHmm

where
   
TYPE:
      RAS ----> RAdiosonde Data 
	CVB ----> Constant Volume Balloon data
	SOD ----> SODar data
	SON ----> SONic data
	GOD ----> Ground Observation Data
      FRW ----> ground observation data from Western France
	NWP ----> Numerical Weather Prediction data from Reading

DATE:
	  MM: month
 	  DD: day
 	  HH: hour
 	  mm: minutes

sometimes file name: TYPEDATE ---- > TYPEMiMiDiDi-MfMf

where 

DATE:
	 MiMi and MfMf indicate month 
 	 DiDi and DiDf indicate day
indices i and j indicate respectively intial and final


The extension _surf and _vert indicate respectively ground level observations 
and upper air observations up to 400 metres.


The extension .D ------> radiosondes from Germany
              .DK -----> .................Danmark
              .SCA ----> .................Scandinavia
                 

